prompt:
This Go function is supposed to run all tasks concurrently and wait for them to finish, but it sometimes prints the same task index several times and sometimes exits early. Explain both problems and give a corrected version.

```go
func runAll(tasks []func(int)) {
    var wg sync.WaitGroup
    for i, t := range tasks {
        go func() {
            wg.Add(1)
            t(i)
            wg.Done()
        }()
    }
    wg.Wait()
}
```
